#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""powos-sleep-gui - Android's cached-app freezer for the Linux apps in the PowOS session (docs/UNIFIED-SLEEP.md).

Runs as the session's user (powos-rooted-session starts it). A KWin script (lib/apps/sleep/kwin, loaded through
KWin's D-Bus /Scripting) reports every app window's focus and minimized state as it changes; nothing here polls.
An app none of whose windows had focus for POWOS_SLEEP_GUI_IDLE (default 10m) is frozen - its whole process tree,
by powos-sleepd (root) - unless:
  - it plays or records audio (a PipeWire stream: pactl's sink-inputs / source-outputs),
  - it moves data: more than 256 KB/s read+written (downloads, uploads, copies) or more than 20% of a core,
  - it's a terminal with a foreground job (a shell whose terminal's foreground group isn't the shell),
  - it, or anything in its tree, is on the never list (powos-sleep-common: the session core, `powos sleep never`),
  - it's one of powos-android-tasks' stand-ins for Android apps (window class android-*),
  - it's a game Steam started (games don't sleep yet).
On the phone "focus" also needs PowOS on screen: the PowOS app showing the desktop or one of its window tasks (the
display daemon's consumers, read from its log - HACK, see Screen). Off screen (Android's home, another app, the
screen off) no window has focus. The desktop shell (plasmashell) itself sleeps while PowOS is off screen
(DESKTOP_IDLE), that process alone, and wakes when PowOS is back, on D-Bus to it, and briefly every 5 minutes.

Apps with a unit of their own (/etc/powos/units.d/<id>.json with "windowClass") get their unit's rule:
  "windowClass": ["steam"]                     its windows (resource class)
  "autosleep": {"idle": "15s"}                 how long unfocused before it sleeps
  "processes": [{"pidfile": P, "tree": true}]  the app is that process's tree, whichever of its processes owns the
                                               window (Steam's windows are steamwebhelper's; the client is the root)
                                               - it stays tracked while it has no window (Steam in the tray)
  "sleepBusy": {"cmdline": "SteamLaunch",      awake while a process of its tree has this in its command line
                "io": "disk", "cpu": false,    busy = disk reads+writes over 256 KB/s (not rchar/wchar: a CEF app's IPC
                                               counts there); its CPU doesn't keep it awake (its idle CPU is the point)
                "startGrace": "2m"}            awake for this long after its root process started (update, login, the
                                               launch it was started for)
Woken by `Wake` (D-Bus dev.powos.Sleep /Gui, `powos-sleep-gui wake <class|pid>`): a launch path (Steam's
/usr/bin/steam, powos-open-task) thaws the app before showing it, so the launch reaches it and not a frozen process.

It thaws at once on focus (activating, raising or un-minimizing it; a notification's click activates it too), and on
any D-Bus message addressed to it (a method call, a notification's targeted ActionInvoked signal, the tray's
Activate): a monitor connection watches only the frozen apps' bus names. Woken by D-Bus while still unfocused, it
sleeps again after a minute.

If this watcher dies, powos-sleepd thaws every GUI app it froze (the connection drops).
"""
